From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hexagonfs: strip a trailing CR from each path segment

The sensor DSP firmware of the Huawei MateBook E Go (SC8280XP) is built
on Windows. When it opens a file through hexagonrpcd, every segment of
the requested path ends in a carriage return, so lookups fail, the DSP
cannot read its sensor registry and no sensors appear.

Strip the CR in copy_segment_and_advance(). It is the common path
parser, so the cleaned segment reaches every backend, the physical
directory backend included, and the served directory needs no file
names with control characters.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs.c b/hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs.c
index bd9f353..4c4b0d6 100644
--- a/hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs.c
+++ b/hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs.c
@@ -56,6 +56,10 @@ static char *copy_segment_and_advance(const char *path,
 
 	memcpy(segment, path, segment_len);
 	segment[segment_len] = 0;
+	/* Firmware built on Windows ends every path segment with a CR. This is the
+	 * common segment parser, so every backend sees the cleaned segment. */
+	if (segment_len > 0 && segment[segment_len - 1] == '\r')
+		segment[--segment_len] = 0;
 
 	*next = next_tmp;
 
